    "ciesin:harvard_doi": "10.7910/DVN/XEFRQ3",
    "ciesin:sedac_doi": "10.7927/H40C4SPR",
    "ciesin:purpose": "To provide a map of wild areas in the Interrupted Goode Homolosine Projection which can be used in wildlife conservation planning, natural resource management, and research on human-environment interactions.",
    "ciesin:supplemental_info": "To reproduce this dataset, the following steps are recommended: 1) Classify the Human Footprint grid according to raster value (wild = 0-10; not wild >10). 2) Eliminate all polygons <5 square kilometers. 3) Select and identify the 10 largest polygon within each biome by realm.",
